Tweeq @VERSION@
================

Tweeq swaps which 3D model an EverQuest race uses, and can enhance EQG models (more polygons,
bigger textures). Everything it changes is reversible: it keeps your original files.

  * Start it from the Tweeq icon on your desktop or in the Start Menu.
  * The first time, Tweeq looks for your EverQuest folder and reads your model files
    (a few minutes; it repeats only after a game patch).
  * Restart EverQuest completely to see changes (the game keeps models cached until it exits).

If Windows says "Windows protected your PC" when you run the installer: Tweeq is free, open
source software and the installer is not signed with a paid certificate yet. Click "More info",
then "Run anyway". You can check the download against the SHA-256 shown on the release page.

Uninstalling: Tweeq offers to put your EverQuest files back to their originals first.
Your settings and the saved originals live in  %APPDATA%\Tweeq  and are kept unless you tell
the uninstaller to delete them.

Tweeq is not affiliated with or endorsed by Daybreak Game Company. EverQuest is a trademark of
Daybreak Game Company LLC. Tweeq contains no EverQuest game files.

